lse,"_score_insider_own":7.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Williams-Sonoma, Inc. operates as an omni-channel specialty retailer of various products for home the United States and internationally. The company provides cooking, dining, and entertaining products, such as cookware, tools, electrics, cutlery, tabletop and bar, outdoor, furniture, and a library of cookbooks. It offers home furnishings, home decor products and accessories, bedding, lighting, rugs, table essentials, kids accessories, made-to-order lighting, hardware, personalized products, custom gifts, and vintage-inspired heirloom products. It offers its products under the Williams Sonoma, Pottery Barn, Pottery Barn Kids, Pottery Barn Teen, West Elm, Williams Sonoma Home, Rejuvenation, Mark and Graham, and GreenRow brand names. The company markets its products through e-commerce websites, direct-mail catalogs, and retail stores. Williams-Sonoma, Inc. was founded in 1956 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Laura J. Alber | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $14.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $394K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $53K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 36\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Williams-Sonoma, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $24.8B market cap on $7.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 106% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 95-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 79% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7929650162492832},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $18.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","19 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Williams-Sonoma (NYSE:WSM) Keep Its Dividend Momentum Going Forward?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/retail/can-williams-sonoma-nysewsm-keep-its-dividend-momentum-going-forward","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795211580.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Williams-Sonoma (NYSE:WSM) Stock Price Target Lowered at Robert W. Baird","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/williams-sonoma-nysewsm-stock-price-target-lowered-at-robert-w-baird.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795180025.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Can Williams-Sonoma (NYSE:WSM) Ride a Solid Quarter Into the Holidays?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/can-williams-sonoma-nysewsm-ride-a-solid-quarter-into-the-holidays","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795155060.0